X0X 1.2.0 BETA – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-x0x tag v1.2.0
(commit ca2d377e3b9522579245152a81781a575f4d2fea; source: https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-x0x/archive/ca2d377e3b9522579245152a81781a575f4d2fea.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. X0X by Charles Vestal, a fork of Felucca: Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments (the platform parts).
Ported parts keep their licences (the 909 after 9W9 / ER-99, the 808 after 8W8, the 303 after schwung-303: Open303 by Robin Schmidt, MIT; TB-3PO after the Phazerville Hemisphere Suite;
the break generator after BB Gen by mestela, by permission; the screen reader's announce.c: MPL-2.0; the UI faces Barlow Semi Condensed and Terminus are rasterised in: OFL 1.1):
X0X's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file. TR-808, TR-909 and TB-303 are trademarks of Roland Corporation. The JieLi SDK files of X0X's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/x0x_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as X0X's own browser emulator does (web/emu/x0x_web.c, host/x0x_host.c)
and adds the device's storage.c on the flash image, the USB SysEx path (editor.c, ota.c's identity handshake, backup.c's backup and restore) and USB MIDI out; the hardware stand-ins are the emulator's:
keys/LEDs/LCD, the MASTER pot, NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, one core, USB = always configured, no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no updater and no USB boot
(ota.c answers the identity handshake only), the default panel map (no hardware calibration). Compiled with WASI SDK clang.

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-x0x at commit ca2d377e3b9522579245152a81781a575f4d2fea
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py and the glue tools/studio/x0x_studio.c. A tarball of exactly this commit
(fm1-x0x-ca2d377e3b9522579245152a81781a575f4d2fea.tar.gz, made with tools/make_source_tarballs.py) is attached to every
FM-1 Companion release that ships this build: https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/releases
Written offer: for at least three years after the last release that ships this build, the maintainers of
FM-1 Companion will give anyone a copy of that corresponding source on request (https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/issues),
free of charge apart from the cost of physically performing the distribution.
